-- Confirmation of Registered Office and Business Address.
--
-- Generated by the Hub (not uploaded by the applicant) when a registered-address
-- membership goes live, and again whenever staff ask for a fresh copy.
--
-- This is a new document_type, not a reuse of registered_address_mandate.
-- The mandate is the client's authority inside the membership agreement.
-- The confirmation letter is the Village Hub letter the client gives to
-- CIPC (CoR21.1), SARS and their bank. Mixing the two would make the
-- documents list and the approval checklist lie about what was signed.
--
-- Postgres will not let a transaction use an enum value added in the same
-- transaction, so this file only adds the value.

alter type document_type add value if not exists 'registered_address_confirmation';
